notes,authority=load('review_notes.json'),load('authority_map.json');assert notes['findings'][-1]['id']=='Q319' and authority['entries'][-1]['id']=='A823'
findings=[
 {'id':'Q320','title':'Saving does not end the undo coalescing run, so another edit can stay falsely clean','source':'crates/cambium/backstep/src/lib.rs:75,138; crates/cambium/scenes/scenomise/src/authoring.rs:353,376','status':'verified original History API with standard-library-only runtime counterexample; editor save caller source traced','evidence':'History::mark_saved records undo.len but leaves last_key/last_time live. Record initial 0 with a field key at t1000, edit to 1, mark_saved, then record 1 under the same key at t1100 and edit to 2: record coalesces without changing depth, is_dirty remains false, and undo(2) returns 0, skipping the saved content 1. Current Scenomise save/load/mark_saved paths call this API without break_run inside those paths. The actual editor UI and persistence were not run. Eight original Backstep tests plus two counterexamples pass.','diagnostics':['backstep_state_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'A save checkpoint must terminate the coalescing run or use a distinct content/history identity. Keep explicit save and undo semantics together; do not merely repaint the dirty indicator.'}},
 {'id':'Q321','title':'Lowering an existing History cap does not enforce the advertised bound','source':'crates/cambium/backstep/src/lib.rs:61,75','status':'verified public API counterexample; no live product cap-resize consumer established','evidence':'with_cap accepts an already populated History and only changes cap. Starting with five undo entries, applying with_cap(1), then recording another edit leaves five undoable entries because record drops only one before pushing one. Thus the stated cap can remain exceeded indefinitely under ordinary one-entry records. This is an API/resource-bound defect; the current editor construction uses a cap before population and no runtime configuration consumer was proven.','diagnostics':['backstep_state_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Trim down to the chosen cap and update the saved checkpoint consistently, either at cap change or before record. Preserve the existing zero-cap meaning.'}},
 {'id':'Q322','title':'Count::combine indexes past every nonempty array and breaks constant sequence metadata','source':'crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequence.rs:34,64','status':'verified actual current Meristem runtime and expected E0080 constant consumer over two exact retained suppliers','evidence':'The combine loop increments idx before matching vals[idx]. It skips vals[0] and reaches vals[N] for every nonempty input. All four singleton Count variants panic, and Count::One.multiple inherits the panic. A separate consumer evaluating public ViewSequence::ELEMENTS_COUNT at compile time fails E0080 on this original source. The ordinary 37 integration and 9 core unit tests pass because they do not evaluate the affected metadata on these shapes. This is a real metadata implementation defect, not evidence that all normal view construction currently fails.','diagnostics':['meristem_state_probe_receipt.json','meristem_original_suite_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Evaluate the current index before incrementing and cover empty/single/mixed counts plus a real sequence constant. Do not interpret normal build success as evaluation of lazy associated constants.'}},
 {'id':'Q323','title':'Vec partial regrowth discards generation tombstones, then revives a stale child route','source':'crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequences/impl_vec.rs:30,175,225','status':'verified actual current generic sequence using its original test element/splice fixture over exact retained suppliers','evidence':'VecSeqState documents retaining generations for the longest-ever sequence. The grow branch unconditionally resize(n,0), which can truncate the generations vector when regrowing below its historical maximum. A real core 3->1->2->3 sequence shows the removed index-2 route correctly stale after shrinking, panicking during partial regrowth when message indexes the truncated vector, then matching generation 0 again after full regrowth. The old child-3 message returns Action(30) from the replacement child. Existing stale tests cover 1->0->1 and miss this path. These are core routing results, not native DOM/application activation or OS event timing.','diagnostics':['meristem_state_probe_receipt.json','meristem_original_suite_probe_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Only extend generation storage beyond its historical maximum; retain removed-slot generations. Also refuse out-of-live-range paths before indexing state, without silently routing a stale payload to a replacement.'}}
]
for f in findings:f['verification']=NAME
notes['findings'].extend(findings)
rows=[
 ('History owns checkpoints but callers also own save boundaries','Backstep offers mark_saved and break_run as independent operations.', ['crates/cambium/backstep/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/scenes/scenomise/src/authoring.rs'], 'Q320 verifies that the saved-depth authority is insufficient when coalescing continues. Scenomise wraps the same shared owner; it does not cure this in its save implementation. Q321 separately bounds the cap API claim, with no live runtime cap consumer established.'),
 ('Command catalogue shares identities, not product execution authority','Command-menu provides canonical IDs and menu grouping while callers provide host commands and enabled reasons.', ['crates/cambium/command-menu/src/catalogue.rs','crates/cambium/command-menu/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/command-menu/src/session.rs'], 'MenuSession::chosen intentionally returns a selected disabled item; an original source test explicitly expects it. A disabled-activation defect needs the actual product run guard traced. CommandChoices serializes stored choices rather than re-deriving graph authority; recent/search lists dedupe stable command IDs. Do not promote a catalogue one-home claim into a claim that every product command executor is shared.'),
 ('Meristem is the generic retained-view owner, not a second DOM','View, ViewSequence, MessageCtx and ElementSplice retain typed app/backend state.', ['crates/cambium/meristem/src/view.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequence.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/element_splice.rs'], 'The backend owns real elements and splice operations. Hoist/extract/adopt defaults explicitly return Unsupported without consuming, with an original passing test. Lens, map-state and map-message have different construction/message responsibilities; matching wrapper shapes alone do not establish duplicate document truth.'),
 ('Stale-message generations have several implementations','Option and AnyView use u64 generations; positional Vec packs u32 index/generation; keyed backends retain their own identity rules.', ['crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequences/impl_option.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequences/impl_vec.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/views/any_view.rs'], 'Q323 proves the positional Vec generation owner violates its own retention rule. Different sequence and erased-view lifecycles justify some separate generation state; the independent recipes still need consistent stale-message refusal. No cross-backend generation equivalence is claimed.'),
 ('Reference wrappers repeat a rebuild policy','Rc and Arc each implement pointer-identity skipping plus RequestRebuild invalidation.', ['crates/cambium/meristem/src/views/impl_rc.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/message_context.rs'], 'The source repeats the same operational policy across two ownership wrappers. Existing Arc tests pass and no behavioral divergence is proven. AnyView Send/Sync variants delegate to a shared dynamic implementation, so three public trait shapes do not mean three erased-view engines.'),
 ('Count metadata has an independent success blind spot','Array, tuple and Vec associated constants depend on shared Count helpers.', ['crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequence.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequences/impl_array.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequences/impl_tuples.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_sequences/impl_vec.rs'], 'Q322 demonstrates runtime panic and const E0080 while all 46 original nonoptional tests pass. Compilation does not demand every associated constant. Preserve the separate expected-failure receipt instead of labeling its nonzero compile exit as a failed fixture.'),
 ('Message-path safety partly remains a trusted caller contract','Typed take/downcast ownership is centralized in MessageCtx; incomplete route checking is a debug assertion.', ['crates/cambium/meristem/src/message_context.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/src/view_ctx.rs'], 'Normal internal routing consumes each path component before leaf delivery. with_id uses push/call/pop and is not unwind-safe by itself. No reuse-after-contained-panic product route was proven, so retain these as contract follow-ups rather than security/runtime findings.'),
 ('Existing test receipts are narrower than the view protocol claims','Original Meristem tests exercise current generic element/splice fixtures.', ['crates/cambium/meristem/tests/base_sequence.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/tests/vec_sequence.rs','crates/cambium/meristem/tests/common/mod.rs'], 'All 37 original integration cases and 9 core unit cases pass over freshly compiled current Meristem and two exact retained suppliers. One Option some-none-some stale test constructs the final view then delivers through the earlier None view; source review alone does not give that test final-view route coverage. No optional kurbo/doc/native app acceptance is claimed.')
]
entries=[{'id':f'A{824+i}','domain':d,'claim':c,'implementations':paths,'assessment':a,'state':'complete source reads; named History/core tests and counterexamples only','verification':NAME} for i,(d,c,paths,a) in enumerate(rows)];authority['entries'].extend(entries)
